        "original_id": "e4b349f1-1e94-5268-a57e-c5d4e365c9e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Definitely Maybe Tour\n- People: Noel Gallagher, Liam Gallagher, Tony McCarroll\n- Songs: Don't Look Back in Anger\n- Places: Gleneagles, Scotland, Sheffield Arena\n\nFacts:\n- The Definitely Maybe Tour started on 6 February 1994 with a short concert at Gleneagles, Scotland.\n- Noel Gallagher wrote the song \"Don't Look Back in Anger.\"\n- The Definitely Maybe Tour ended on 22 April 1995 at the Sheffield Arena.\n- The 22 April 1995 Sheffield Arena concert featured the acoustic debut of the future hit \"Don't Look Back in Anger.\"\n- The 22 April 1995 Sheffield Arena concert was the last concert to feature original drummer Tony McCarroll.\n- \"Don't Look Back in Anger\" was the first Oasis single with lead vocals by Noel Gallagher instead of Liam Gallagher, although Noel Gallagher had previously sung lead only on B-sides.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ae6c60f8-a093-5ada-a435-5b5512a92734",
        "text": "Page: Definitely Maybe Tour. Sentence: The tour started on 6 February 1994 with a short concert at Gleneagles, Scotland, and ended on 22 April 1995 at the Sheffield Arena, which featured an acoustic debut of the future hit Don't Look Back in Anger and was also the last concert to feature original drummer Tony McCarroll.\nPage: Don't Look Back in Anger. Sentence: The song was written by the band's guitarist and main songwriter, Noel Gallagher.\nPage: Don't Look Back in Anger. Sentence: \"Don't Look Back in Anger\" was also the first Oasis single with lead vocals by Noel (who had previously only sung lead on B-sides) instead of his brother, Liam.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
